# Line endings. Every text file in this repository is stored with LF — all 77
# tracked text files already are — and Git converts on the way in and out so a
# Windows editor can go on writing CRLF without it ever reaching a commit.
#
# Without this file the conversion depends on each machine's core.autocrlf, and
# the first person to clone with it unset commits a file with CRLF in it. Then
# every later diff of that file is the whole file.

* text=auto

# Files Windows itself reads. cmd.exe parses a .bat line by line and has been
# known to mis-handle a label or a multi-line block in an LF-only file, and the
# installer's PowerShell is run by Windows PowerShell 5.1, not pwsh. These are
# small and Windows-only; give them the endings Windows expects.
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf

# Files something other than a human parses, where a stray CR is a bug:
# GitHub Actions runs the workflow on Linux tooling as well as Windows, and
# public_key.txt is read as bytes and base64-decoded.
*.yml                    text eol=lf
*.yaml                   text eol=lf
packaging/public_key.txt text eol=lf

# Binary: never convert, never try to diff. icon.ico and icon.png are the two
# in the tree today; the rest are here so an asset added later is safe by
# default rather than corrupted by an eol conversion nobody asked for.
*.ico   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp4   binary
*.mkv   binary
*.mp3   binary
*.flac  binary
*.zip   binary
*.7z    binary
*.exe   binary
*.dll   binary
*.db    binary
